    },
    {
     "clause": "A governed-deleted generation is closed. At the fact level (`dispute` of a tombstoned fact by its uuid, a governed pruning of one of its versions, the adapter's delete of a member of a deleted lineage) the answer is `already_deleted`; at the facade's logical-reference level (`forget`, permanent `forget`, `correct`, `dispute` by `target_reference`) the former owner reads the bare `fact_not_found` result, because the reference has no visible head. Either answer is the same whether or not another scope has since re-created the id, and neither moves or reads the live generation [...] The one further governed act is the escalation of a reversible pruning to a permanent deletion by a writer eligible for that generation: it keeps the tombstone's `deleted_at`, recorded version and lineage, erases the content, and neither reads nor moves a live generation another scope holds.",
